prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for DeKalb County runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. January to February and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those years. In 2025 November to December ran 40% of normal on the middle of the grids, while May to June hit 173%. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, and grid 16977 bottomed out at 55%.</p>"}
